Hi Scott & Håvard,

Many thanks for raising this issue and looking into it. I wondered if the latest testing version had fixed the issue for Scott? I have a similar issue that appeared after updating INLA and switching from sp to sf workflows (haven't managed to identify which caused it to start).

I'm currently working on trying to get the testing version working. When trying to run, the pardiso.license argument seems to have been dropped from the inla.setOption function in the latest version? Subsequently trying to run without pardiso causes a version `GLIBC_2.29' not found error message on the cluster. Is there another way to specify the pardiso licence?

Kind regards,
Charles

