Hi,

I think I might have located the cause of this problem.

The posterior estimates are almost the same with and without specification on the prior means of the fixed effects. It seems like the prior means have not been taken into account properly (and its always centered around 0), maybe due to some coding errors.

See following for codes:

library(INLA)
y1 <- rnorm(n = 10000, mean = 3.5, sd = 1)

prec <- runif(1, 0, 1e5)
fit1 <- inla(y1 ~ 1, data = as_tibble(y1)
             ,control.fixed = list(mean.intercept = 3.5, prec.intercept = prec))

fit2 <- inla(y1 ~ 1, data = as_tibble(y1)

             ,control.fixed = list(prec.intercept = prec))

fit1$all.hyper$fixed
fit1$summary.fixed
fit2$all.hyper$fixed
fit2$summary.fixed

Kai

